
stringstream

- Used to treat a string as an input/output stream.
- Converts strings to numbers and vice versa.
- Splits a string into tokens separated by whitespace.
- Works similarly to cin and cout but on strings.

Common uses:
1. Parse a line containing multiple values.
2. Convert string -> int/double.
3. Build a formatted string.

Example:
string s = "10 20 30";
stringstream ss(s);

int x;
while (ss >> x)
{
    // Reads: 10, 20, 30
}


